# 110. Explicit Non-Goals for Initial V1

Unless separately approved, V1 does not require:

* Automated payment gateway
* Automated customer checkout
* Fully automated sales onboarding
* Automated email sales workflow
* SSO
* Enterprise identity federation
* Complex billing automation
* Automatic service-model migration without controlled approval
* Private/self-hosted deployment

These may be future roadmap features.

---

# 111. Critical Business Rules

The following rules are authoritative.

### Rule A

There is exactly one Super Admin authority.

### Rule B

Every customer is represented by an Organization.

### Rule C

Every Organization has exactly one active Service Model.

### Rule D

V1 active Service Models are:

```text
MANAGED
CUSTOMER_DB
```

Private is not active in V1.

### Rule E

Service Model and Package are different concepts.

### Rule F

Super Admin controls the Organization's commercial subscription.

### Rule G

Organization Admin cannot independently modify Super Admin-owned subscription terms.

### Rule H

Manual payment is the initial payment method.

### Rule I

Super Admin can pause and resume organizations.

### Rule J

Agent capability must be server-authorized.

### Rule K

Tenant isolation is mandatory.

### Rule L

Important state changes must be audited.

### Rule M

No silent service-model changes.

### Rule N

No silent destructive deletion.

### Rule O

Production functionality must not depend on fake/random data.

### Rule P

There is one Universal OmniSight Agent architecture.

### Rule Q

The Universal Agent must remain OmniSight-centric.

### Rule R

The Universal Agent must not contain customer database/storage credentials.

### Rule S

Organization data destination must be resolved server-side.

### Rule T

Customer DB deployments use customer-controlled database and customer-controlled storage for applicable organization-owned data.

### Rule U

An Organization Admin may request infrastructure changes but cannot activate them independently.

### Rule V

Super Admin approval is required before an infrastructure change becomes active.

### Rule W

Infrastructure changes must be validated before activation.

### Rule X

Where existing organization data is affected by a service-model migration, that data must be migrated and verified before cutover.

### Rule Y

Migration must provide controlled failure handling and rollback where technically feasible.

### Rule Z

Platform/global data remains platform-owned and must not be indiscriminately moved into customer infrastructure.

---

# 112. Future Extension Model

The architecture should allow future additions without changing the fundamental hierarchy.

Possible future additions:

```text
More Packages
More Feature Entitlements
Automated Billing
Payment Gateway
Email Automation
2FA
SSO
Advanced Analytics
AI Intelligence
Additional Agent Platforms
Additional Storage Providers
Additional Database Providers
Additional Deployment Models
Private / Self-Hosted Enterprise
```

Future functionality must extend the existing model rather than bypass it.

---

# 113. Future Private Deployment

Private/self-hosted deployment is a future consideration only.

If introduced in a future version, it must receive a separate approved architecture and contract.

It must NOT be treated as a hidden V1 feature.

Future Private architecture may eventually require:

* Application deployment
* API deployment
* Database setup
* Storage setup
* Environment configuration
* Network requirements
* Reverse proxy
* TLS
* Backup
* Upgrade process
* License validation
* Support/update mechanism

This section does not authorize Private deployment in V1.

---

# 114. Final Product Architecture — V1

The intended OmniSight V1 architecture is:

```text
                             OMNISIGHT
                                 │
               ┌─────────────────┴──────────────────┐
               │                                    │
         SUPER ADMIN                           PUBLIC LANDING
               │
       ┌───────┼──────────┐
       │       │          │
 Organizations Packages Settings
       │
       ├───────────────────────────────┐
       │                               │
 Service Model                    Subscription
       │                               │
   ┌───┴───────────┐              ┌────┴─────┐
   │               │              │          │
 MANAGED       CUSTOMER_DB     Payment    Invoice
   │               │
   │               │
   │         Customer DB
   │               +
   │         Customer Storage
   │
   └──────────┬──────────────┘
              │
       Organization
              │
      ┌───────┼───────────────┐
      │       │               │
    Admin   Manager         Viewer
      │
  Employees
      │
Universal Agents
      │
OmniSight API
      │
Server-side Organization Resolver
      │
 ┌────┴──────────────────────┐
 │                           │
Managed Destination     Customer Destination
 │                           │
OmniSight DB             Customer DB
     +                         +
OmniSight Storage        Customer Storage
```

---

# 115. Final Universal Agent Architecture

The canonical Agent architecture is:

```text
                  UNIVERSAL OMNISIGHT AGENT
                              │
              ┌───────────────┼────────────────┐
              │               │                │
        Device Identity   Secure Auth       Config
              │               │                │
              └───────────────┼────────────────┘
                              │
                        OmniSight API
                              │
                  Server-side Organization
                         Resolution
                              │
                 ┌────────────┴────────────┐
                 │                         │
              MANAGED                  CUSTOMER_DB
                 │                         │
          OmniSight DB              Customer DB
                 │                         │
          OmniSight Storage        Customer Storage
```

The Agent never directly decides between these destinations.

The Agent never receives customer database/storage credentials.

The Agent only communicates with OmniSight.

---

# 116. Final Customer Infrastructure Migration Architecture

The canonical migration architecture is:

```text
CURRENT DESTINATION
        │
        ↓
CHANGE REQUEST
        │
        ↓
VALIDATION
        │
        ↓
SUPER ADMIN APPROVAL
        │
        ↓
DATA MIGRATION
        │
        ├── Structured Data → Customer DB
        │
        └── Binary Data → Customer Storage
        │
        ↓
VERIFICATION
        │
        ↓
CONTROLLED CUTOVER
        │
        ↓
NEW ACTIVE DESTINATION
        │
        ↓
SAFETY / ROLLBACK WINDOW
        │
        ↓
OLD DESTINATION RETIREMENT
```

The old destination must not be destroyed before successful verification and the applicable safety/retention period.

---

# 117. Final Web ↔ Agent Relationship

The relationship between Web/Control Plane and Agent is:

```text
Web / Control Plane
        │
        ├── Organization
        ├── Subscription
        ├── Package
        ├── Entitlement
        ├── Policy
        ├── Agent Identity
        ├── Device Identity
        └── Data Destination
                 │
                 ↓
             OmniSight API
                 │
                 ↓
        Universal OmniSight Agent
```

The Agent is an execution component.

The server is the authority.

---

# 118. Final Product Statement — V1

OmniSight is a Super Admin-controlled multi-organization SaaS/service platform.

The commercial model is based on:

```text
Customer
    ↓
Organization
    ↓
Service Model
    ↓
Package
    ↓
Subscription
    ↓
Manual Payment
    ↓
Organization Users
    ↓
Universal OmniSight Agent
    ↓
OmniSight API
    ↓
Server-side Data Destination Resolution
    ↓
Monitoring & Operational Data
```

The two official V1 OmniSight Service Models are:

```text
1. OmniSight Managed
2. Customer Database
```

For Customer Database organizations, the intended sensitive-data architecture is:

```text
Customer Database
+
Customer Storage
```

Private/self-hosted deployment is NOT part of V1 and must not be exposed in:

* UI
* APIs
* Agent Builder
* provisioning
* customer workflows
* V1 documentation presented as an active option

The OmniSight Agent architecture is Universal.

There is one Universal OmniSight Agent.

The Agent is OmniSight-centric and communicates with the OmniSight API.

The Agent must not contain customer database or customer storage credentials.

The Agent must not directly select or connect to a customer database or customer storage system.

OmniSight's server-side organization resolver determines the correct data destination.

For Managed organizations:

```text
OmniSight API
    ↓
OmniSight DB
+
OmniSight Storage
```

For Customer Database organizations:

```text
OmniSight API
    ↓
Customer DB
+
Customer Storage
```

Organization infrastructure changes are controlled operations.

An Organization Admin may submit a database/storage change request.

The requested destination must be validated.

Super Admin approval is mandatory.

Where existing organization data is affected, migration must be performed before cutover.

Migration must be verified.

Only after successful verification may the new destination become active.

Rollback must be supported where technically feasible.

The previous destination must not be immediately deleted after migration.

Platform/global data remains platform-owned.

Organization-owned operational data follows the organization's active service-model data destination.

The Super Admin is the final authority over:

* platform configuration
* organizations
* service models
* packages
* subscriptions
* payments
* Agent provisioning
* infrastructure approval
* migration approval
* platform policies

Organization Admins operate their own organizations but cannot override platform-owned commercial or deployment decisions.

The system must enforce:

* security
* tenant isolation
* explicit state transitions
* auditable operations
* subscription-aware access
* server-authoritative Agent capabilities
* server-authoritative organization binding
* secure infrastructure credential management
* controlled data migration
* verification
* safe cutover
* rollback
* privacy-aware monitoring
* production-grade reliability

This document is the Master Product Definition and must be used as the baseline for all future OmniSight implementation work.

---

# 119. Master PRD Authority Statement

This version supersedes conflicting earlier architectural assumptions regarding:

* separate Agent variants
* Agent-controlled customer infrastructure
* Agent-held customer DB credentials
* Agent-held customer storage credentials
* direct Agent-to-customer-database connections
* direct Agent-to-customer-storage connections
* uncontrolled service-model changes
* immediate infrastructure switching
* unverified data migration
* V1 Private deployment

The authoritative V1 architecture is:

```text
ONE UNIVERSAL AGENT
        ↓
OMNISIGHT API
        ↓
SERVER-SIDE ORGANIZATION RESOLUTION
        ↓
MANAGED OR CUSTOMER-CONTROLLED DATA DESTINATION
```

This architecture is the canonical OmniSight V1 implementation direction.
